A||N||5||grinthock||WHAT A WEEKEND - FIERO LUCK!||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||08-26-2001||10:18 PM||||Well guys I can hardly type this, what a AMAZING weekend I had, other than I REALLY REALLY wanted to goto the PA BBQ it was perfect.<P><BR>First, Saturday morn I got up, FELT GREAT, headed up north towards my home town of Barrie (north of TORONTO), stopped on the way at COOKSTOWN AUTO WRECKERS.  HUGE lot there, I need a front manifold.  I walk into the lot and there is a nice row of 8 fieros, stripped good, 3 engine cradles on the ground though.   Sitting beside one with the nuts pretty much already off is a GOOD FRONT MANIFOLD with X-OVER!! What luck, BUT there is one bolt holding it all on, and I forgot to bring the tools.<P>2 other people were walking around the fieros, one approaced and offered assistance.  I thanked him, he asked me if I knew of pennocks, I said sure, I told him who I was.   IT WAS OLIVER SCHOLZ!  Anyone who doesn't know him he makes fiero electronics, scantool, HUD, onboard computer.  About  year ago Oliver and I over email had produced/designed the fiero digital speedo/tach project which is now on his WWW, but I had never met him!  AND HERE HE WAS, in hte middle of a junk yard that is about 30 miles from any civilization here in CANADA!<P>What a fluke, well Oliver, I had a great time chatting with you, it was great meeting you even if it WAS under the weirdest circumstances.<P>Back to the manifold, the wrecker ended up giving me the Manifold AND the X-Over pipe for $25 CDN!  WHAT A DEAL!<P>That's the fiero part.<P>That night I went to the drive in with a buddy who owns a car audio shop, 20 minutes before we left we rigged up one of the 32" (yes 32") Clarion Sub woofers into the company VAN to take to the movies.  It was great for 20 mintues of the movie "Rush Hour 2" until people started complaining to the management that our BASS was too loud.  It sounded like a real theatre.  IT was amazing.<P><BR>Well that's pretty much my weekend, now onto the weekday and my car.||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||08-26-2001||10:24 PM||||Hey Grint,  Sorry too you didn't make the BBQ. Here is a link to some of what you missed.  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009803.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009803.html</A> <P>I hope you get your Fiero purring soon.  Sound like it was suppose to be that you couldn't make it to the PA BBQ.  What is Olivers web site address?  <P>Good hearing from you,<P>Skitime<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
